part.text:
Modify tail strands. Replace the loop of 4 cones with 14 curved strands. Also update tail hair mass maybe. Current `TailHairMass` tube from [0,1.24,0.68] to [0,1.33,0.28] with radii. Keep, then add strands:
```
for (let strand=0; strand<14; strand++){
  const t = strand/13;
  const x = (t-0.5)*0.20; // spread across width
  const side = x>=0?1:-1;
  const length = 0.42 + ((strand*7)%5)*0.035;
  const points = [
    [x*0.35, 1.26, 0.66],
    [x*0.55 + side*0.01, 1.31, 0.55],
    [x*0.75 + side*0.02, 1.33, 0.42],
    [x, 1.30 + (t-0.5)*0.10, 0.40 - length*0.55],
  ];
  radii [0.026,0.020,0.012,0.002]
  attach Tail5
}
```
Need the tail hair to hang down; z from 0.66 to ~0.15. The horse hocks at 0.46; a long tail to 0.15 is near the ground; real tail ends around hocks/ground. Use lengths 0.35-0.55 → end z 0.2-0.1. Good.
- Add a few shorter strands from Tail4 (upper) to blend. Maybe not.

Let's replace the 4-strand loop.

